#41003
"Road Through Light Woods"
"Mottled trunks of thin beech rise around the road, sprouting from between old,

moss-covered stumps.  Through the thin forest structures are visible to the

west.  Uphill, undergrowth knots tightly between older trees.  The road is

heavily rutted with dried remnants of puddles forming muddy bogs in the cart

tracks.

